# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signing secrets - NEVER commit these.
#
# Apple signing artefacts (Distribution cert, App Store Connect API
# key, provisioning profile) and Android keystores are sensitive
# enough that a leak forces an immediate revocation + regeneration
# cycle and could compromise the published app's integrity. We
# protect them at three layers:
#   1. The explicit `secrets/` folder where humans drop the files.
#   2. Per-extension globs (so a `.p8` left elsewhere by mistake is
#      still ignored).
#   3. The rotated `*-credentials.zip` bundles we sometimes use to
#      ship a full set to the CI vault.
# All of these are also stored in the Pollen 1Password vault; the
# repo only ever sees the raw files transiently.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
secrets/
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.jks
*.keystore
*-credentials.zip
*-service-account.json
